  "lineage": "Non-film Tamil popular music took shape in the 1990s when the Chennai studio culture around Ilaiyaraaja and A. R. Rahman spilled into standalone albums — Unnikrishnan and Bombay Jayashri's light-music records, then the 2000s Tamil rock and indie wave (Kadal Pura, Anthony Daasan) and after 2015 an internet-native scene of Hiphop Tamizha, Sean Roldan and Santhosh Narayanan side projects — typically 80-130 BPM 4/4 productions blending programmed kits and synth pads with mridangam, thavil, nadaswaram or urumi accents and Carnatic-trained vocal gamaka over Western chord progressions.",
